<p>"Which mark is necessary on electrical appliances?" "Which safety mark is standard on helmets?" These questions appear in exams, but also on the desks of importers and manufacturers deciding what to print on a label.</p>
<p><strong>The short answer:</strong> most safety-critical goods in India need a <strong>BIS mark</strong>. Products such as helmets, appliances, fans and cement use the <strong>ISI mark</strong>, and electronics and IT goods use the <strong>Standard Mark with an R-number under CRS</strong>. Energy-using products may also need a <strong>BEE star label</strong>, and gold jewellery needs a <strong>BIS hallmark</strong>.</p>
<p>Below is a product-by-product guide, followed by a quick way to check any product yourself.</p>

